  "id": "COMPOUND:38301 - PROTEIN:5867",
  "verbalization": "Hedaol B is shown to have a target relationship with HaCaT through multiple pathways, all of which involve the same chemical compound, (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol. This compound is identified as a target of Hedaol B in three distinct contexts: HepG2, A549, and SQ20B. All three cell lines are known to be targets of this compound, and the shared target relationship with HaCaT suggests a potential mechanism of action involving this compound. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Hedaol B and HaCaT through the inhibition of a common target, which may underlie the observed effects. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-characterized compound in multiple cell lines, indicating a possible role in cellular processes that are relevant to HaCaT. The integration of these findings suggests that Hedaol B may act through a mechanism involving this compound, potentially affecting cellular pathways in HaCaT cells.",
